================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

Saito's own code is under the MIT License above. A release distribution also
carries third-party code, each under its own license — this section names what
the distribution physically contains, not the wider dependency tree a developer
installs.

PHP dependencies (`vendor/`)

    Installed by Composer for a production build (`composer install --no-dev`).
    Each package keeps its own license file under `vendor/<vendor>/<package>/`;
    they are predominantly MIT, BSD-3-Clause and Apache-2.0. CakePHP, the
    framework Saito is built on, is MIT.

Front-end libraries (compiled into `webroot/js` and `webroot/css`)

    Bootstrap 4.6.2 .......................... MIT
    Alpine.js 3 .............................. MIT
    htmx 2 ................................... BSD Zero Clause (0BSD)
    Font Awesome 4.7.0 ....................... code MIT; fonts SIL OFL 1.1

Bundled fonts (shipped under `plugins/*/webroot/fonts`)

    Cabin .................................... SIL Open Font License 1.1
    Fenix .................................... SIL Open Font License 1.1

    The SIL OFL requires its text to travel with the fonts; it is shipped as
    `OFL.txt` beside them (and kept in the repository at
    `webroot/css/src/fonts/OFL.txt`).
